Q. After what number of nodes in the internal working of the HashMap does the linkedlist
converts to tree ?And what is the term called?

Ans: 🔷 1️⃣ When does LinkedList become Tree?

     👉 In a HashMap, when too many elements go into the same bucket, it converts:

     LinkedList → Red-Black Tree

     ✅ Threshold value
     👉
     8 (TREEIFY_THRESHOLD)

     Meaning:

     If number of nodes in a bucket ≥ 8

     👉 Then:
     ✔ LinkedList → Tree (Red-Black Tree)


     🔷 2️⃣ When does it convert back to LinkedList?
     👉
     6 (UNTREEIFY_THRESHOLD)

     If nodes drop below 6:

     ✔ Tree → LinkedList


     🔷 3️⃣ Important Condition (VERY IMPORTANT 🔥)

     👉 Tree conversion happens ONLY IF:

     HashMap size ≥ 64

     👉 Constant:
     MIN_TREEIFY_CAPACITY = 64

     ❗ If size < 64

     👉 Instead of tree:
     ✔ HashMap resizes (rehashing happens)

     🔷 4️⃣ What is the “index” called?

     👉 The term used is:

     ✅ Bucket Index

     How index is calculated:
     index = (n - 1) & hash

     Where:
     n = size of array
     hash = hashCode of key

     👉 This index tells:

     “Which bucket (position) this key goes into”

     🔷 5️⃣ Full Internal Flow
     Key → hashCode()
     Hash → index (bucket index)

     If collision:
     Add to LinkedList

     If nodes ≥ 8:
     Convert to Tree (if capacity ≥ 64)

     🔷 6️⃣ Why Tree is used?

     👉 LinkedList:
     Search = O(n)

     👉 Tree:
     Search = O(log n)

     🔷 7️⃣ Summary Table

     Concept	                                                      Value

     Treeify threshold	                                              8
     Untreeify threshold	                                          6
     Min capacity for tree	                                          64

     Index term	                                                     Bucket Index

     🔷 🔥 Interview Answer
     👉
     In HashMap (Java 8+), when the number of elements in a bucket exceeds 8, the linked list is
     converted into a balanced tree (Red-Black Tree), provided the overall capacity is at least 64.
     The index used to store elements is called the bucket index, which is calculated using the hash
     of the key.

     🔷 One-line memory trick

     👉
     8 → Tree, 6 → Back, 64 → Condition